meta {
  name: Create Request - duplicate
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{apiUrl}}/requests
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{idToken2}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "sessionId": "{{sessionId}}"
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 409
  res.body.success: eq false
  res.body.error.code: eq DUPLICATE_REQUEST
}

docs {
  Implemented (D3). Run **Create Request** first (as the player), then this, as the
  **same player** -- a duplicate only exists if it's the same `PK`+`SK`
  (`SESSION#<id>` / `REQUEST#USER#<playerId>`), so this must use `{{idToken2}}`, not the
  host's token.

  `request.repository.ts`'s `create()` catches `ConditionalCheckFailedException` from its
  condition expression and throws `DuplicateRequestError` -> 409. That condition's `OR`
  half lets a `WITHDRAWN` request's item be overwritten by a fresh join (see **Host
  Decisions / Create Request - rejoin inside cooldown** for the rate-limit check that now
  also guards that path), so this test specifically needs the request to still be *live*
  (`PENDING` here) for the duplicate guard to actually fire.
}
